1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,398
Last time, the harbormaster called,

2
00:00:02,848 --> 00:00:05,645
and all the crew could do was listen.

3
00:00:06,545 --> 00:00:08,114
Today they get to answer.

4
00:00:09,014 --> 00:00:10,777
One answer asks her for more,

5
00:00:11,227 --> 00:00:12,757
one takes on a quest,

6
00:00:13,207 --> 00:00:14,217
and one hangs up.

7
00:00:16,017 --> 00:00:18,597
And the answer they give changes the story.

8
00:00:19,797 --> 00:00:22,398
Here's her call on Comms, after Continue.

9
00:00:23,298 --> 00:00:25,463
Under her question there's a list of answers,

10
00:00:25,913 --> 00:00:28,713
two rows at a time, with a scroll bar for the rest,

11
00:00:29,163 --> 00:00:30,662
and the crew picks one.

12
00:00:32,462 --> 00:00:34,651
In the file, an answer is one line,

13
00:00:35,101 --> 00:00:36,718
and you already know its shape.

14
00:00:37,618 --> 00:00:39,414
It's a dash and a space,

15
00:00:39,864 --> 00:00:41,870
then the words in square brackets,

16
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:45,280
then round brackets, with no space between.

17
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:47,836
It's a heading's name and key,

18
00:00:48,286 --> 00:00:50,558
with a dash where the hashes go.

19
00:00:52,358 --> 00:00:55,603
The square brackets hold what Comms reads and picks.

20
00:00:56,503 --> 00:00:59,859
The round brackets say where the conversation goes next,

21
00:01:00,309 --> 00:01:02,923
and when they're empty, the call is over.

22
00:01:04,123 --> 00:01:06,171
Now I put a key in those round brackets,

23
00:01:06,621 --> 00:01:08,691
the key of a scene I haven't written yet.

24
00:01:09,591 --> 00:01:10,840
And lint tells me so:

25
00:01:11,290 --> 00:01:13,967
this answer points at something that isn't there.

26
00:01:15,767 --> 00:01:17,561
Here's what it leads to on Comms:

27
00:01:18,011 --> 00:01:20,710
Quill's offer, with two answers of its own.

28
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:24,022
So I write it, at the end of the file.

29
00:01:24,922 --> 00:01:27,625
It's a scene like the first one, with three hashes,

30
00:01:28,075 --> 00:01:30,763
but it has no When line and no title.

31
00:01:31,663 --> 00:01:33,986
Nothing in the story places it as a call.

32
00:01:34,886 --> 00:01:37,059
The only way in is the answer that names it.

33
00:01:38,259 --> 00:01:41,519
A conversation can branch, and it can come back together.

34
00:01:42,419 --> 00:01:45,276
On Comms, a crew can ask her what she knows,

35
00:01:45,726 --> 00:01:47,731
and she tells them about the gate.

36
00:01:48,631 --> 00:01:50,320
So I add that answer,

37
00:01:50,770 --> 00:01:52,350
and I write the scene for it.

38
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:56,316
And from there, one answer leads on to the same offer.

39
00:01:58,116 --> 00:02:01,033
So a crew that asks first hears a little more,

40
00:02:01,483 --> 00:02:03,132
and ends up in the same place.

41
00:02:04,032 --> 00:02:06,745
Just don't write more than four answers in a scene,

42
00:02:07,195 --> 00:02:09,346
because a fifth is never offered.

43
00:02:10,546 --> 00:02:13,354
So far an answer moves the conversation,

44
00:02:13,804 --> 00:02:15,334
or it ends it.

45
00:02:16,234 --> 00:02:19,246
Now one is going to change the story.

46
00:02:20,146 --> 00:02:22,605
First I need the quest she's offering.

47
00:02:23,505 --> 00:02:26,831
Here it is in the Quest Log, once the crew says yes:

48
00:02:27,281 --> 00:02:29,817
Tag the Hulk, with her face under its order.

49
00:02:30,717 --> 00:02:32,877
I write it up here among my quests.

50
00:02:33,777 --> 00:02:35,558
It starts when revealed,

51
00:02:36,008 --> 00:02:39,570
which keeps it hidden until something starts it.

52
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:44,239
Its description is the quest as Quill gives it.

53
00:02:45,139 --> 00:02:50,009
So it opens with her face, copied from her record,

54
00:02:50,459 --> 00:02:52,390
the way Close Inspection does.

55
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:54,928
Then comes what she wants,

56
00:02:55,378 --> 00:02:58,617
and, after a blank line, why it can't wait.

57
00:03:00,417 --> 00:03:02,624
Lint warns me that nothing does,

58
00:03:03,074 --> 00:03:04,446
and look what it lists:

59
00:03:04,896 --> 00:03:06,965
a Then line, or an answer.

60
00:03:07,865 --> 00:03:11,032
So lint already knows where this is going.

61
00:03:11,932 --> 00:03:13,179
I go back to the offer,

62
00:03:13,629 --> 00:03:16,492
and after the round brackets I type a semicolon,

63
00:03:16,942 --> 00:03:18,960
then accepts, and the quest's key.

64
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:23,173
Everything after that semicolon is what the answer does.

65
00:03:24,373 --> 00:03:26,207
An answer can do two things,

66
00:03:26,657 --> 00:03:29,238
with one semicolon, and a comma between them.

67
00:03:30,138 --> 00:03:33,077
Whichever way the crew answers, they've answered her,

68
00:03:33,527 --> 00:03:35,303
so I mark that moment done as well.

69
00:03:37,103 --> 00:03:39,739
There are four words you can write after the semicolon.

70
00:03:40,639 --> 00:03:42,630
Accepts starts a quest,

71
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:45,293
completes finishes one and pays it,

72
00:03:45,743 --> 00:03:47,146
fails does what it says,

73
00:03:47,596 --> 00:03:50,815
and signal sends a word into the story.

74
00:03:52,015 --> 00:03:54,527
What the crew said can come back to them later.

75
00:03:55,427 --> 00:03:57,559
Here's Comms when the beacon is set:

76
00:03:58,009 --> 00:04:01,522
she calls again, under the title Your beacon.

77
00:04:02,422 --> 00:04:03,618
That takes three pieces.

78
00:04:04,518 --> 00:04:07,234
Watch lint walk me from each one to the next.

79
00:04:09,034 --> 00:04:11,252
First, a Then line on the quest,

80
00:04:11,702 --> 00:04:14,788
and lint says it reveals something that isn't there.

81
00:04:15,688 --> 00:04:18,077
So I write that, a beat like last time's,

82
00:04:18,527 --> 00:04:21,535
and lint says the beat calls a scene that isn't there.

83
00:04:22,435 --> 00:04:24,742
So I write the scene, and now it's clean.

84
00:04:26,542 --> 00:04:27,822
And here's the point of it.

85
00:04:28,722 --> 00:04:32,237
Only a crew that took the quest, and finished it,

86
00:04:32,687 --> 00:04:33,884
ever hears this call.

87
00:04:35,084 --> 00:04:39,565
So that's two ways to make an answer depend on the story.

88
00:04:40,465 --> 00:04:43,574
You put it in a scene that only one answer leads to,

89
00:04:44,023 --> 00:04:47,111
or in a call that only comes later.

90
00:04:48,911 --> 00:04:50,694
You'll see a third way in other pages,

91
00:04:51,144 --> 00:04:53,484
a condition written on the answer itself.

92
00:04:54,384 --> 00:04:56,274
Don't use it in this mission.

93
00:04:57,174 --> 00:04:59,344
It can't read your quests or your credits,

94
00:04:59,794 --> 00:05:02,336
so the answer would never be offered,

95
00:05:02,786 --> 00:05:04,222
and lint can't tell.

96
00:05:05,122 --> 00:05:07,457
We'll use it properly in lecture six,

97
00:05:07,907 --> 00:05:09,597
on a ship's standing.

98
00:05:10,797 --> 00:05:12,717
In we go, and here's her call.

99
00:05:13,617 --> 00:05:15,086
She asks her question,

100
00:05:15,536 --> 00:05:18,286
and now there are three answers in the list.

101
00:05:19,186 --> 00:05:20,884
It shows two rows at a time,

102
00:05:21,334 --> 00:05:22,834
so I scroll down for the rest.

103
00:05:23,734 --> 00:05:25,585
I'll ask what she knows first,

104
00:05:26,035 --> 00:05:27,817
then I tell her the hulk is cold,

105
00:05:28,267 --> 00:05:29,536
and there's the offer.

106
00:05:31,336 --> 00:05:32,431
We will tag her.

107
00:05:33,331 --> 00:05:34,412
The call is over,

108
00:05:34,862 --> 00:05:37,312
and the quest is in the Quest Log,

109
00:05:37,762 --> 00:05:39,567
with Quill's face under its order.

110
00:05:40,467 --> 00:05:43,111
Thirty seconds later it's done and paid,

111
00:05:43,561 --> 00:05:44,885
and she's calling back.

112
00:05:46,085 --> 00:05:47,214
Now the other roads.

113
00:05:48,114 --> 00:05:49,755
If I tell her to find someone else,

114
00:05:50,205 --> 00:05:52,602
there's no quest, and no second call.

115
00:05:53,502 --> 00:05:56,031
And if I scroll down and say not now,

116
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:58,526
the call is gone, and it doesn't come back.

117
00:06:00,326 --> 00:06:02,868
But Back is a different thing.

118
00:06:03,768 --> 00:06:06,242
It puts the call back in the list, unanswered,

119
00:06:06,692 --> 00:06:08,411
and nothing in the story changes.

120
00:06:09,311 --> 00:06:11,732
So the crew always has a way to wait.

121
00:06:12,632 --> 00:06:14,715
Only write an answer that hangs up

122
00:06:15,165 --> 00:06:17,847
when your story can go on without the call.

123
00:06:19,047 --> 00:06:22,062
Now it's your turn: give your second call some answers.

124
00:06:22,962 --> 00:06:25,609
Make one of them send a word into the story,

125
00:06:26,059 --> 00:06:28,545
and write a quest that waits for that word.

126
00:06:30,345 --> 00:06:34,109
Next time, a step the crew can only finish by reporting in.
